---
import Brand from "../../components/Brand.astro";
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { config, prices, formatPrice } from "../../config";
---
<Legal title="Subscription terms" description="Terms for olacare, the subscription that powers the AI assistant.">
  <p>
    <Brand name="care" /> is the subscription that powers the AI voice assistant on your <Brand name="watch" />. The watch's assistant
    does not answer without an active <Brand name="care" /> subscription.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Price and free period</h2>
  <p>
    <Brand name="care" /> costs {formatPrice(prices.care.GBP, "GBP")} per month (UK) or {formatPrice(prices.care.EUR, "EUR")} per
    month (EU), including VAT. It starts with a free {prices.trialMonths}-month trial. When you buy the watch you pay for the
    watch only and agree that we save your card for <Brand name="care" />; nothing is charged for it then. The free trial starts
    when you first pair your watch with your ola account. After the trial it renews automatically every month and your
    saved card is charged, unless you cancel before the trial ends. If your account already had a <Brand name="care" />
    subscription or free trial, or has complimentary access, no new free trial applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Saving your card</h2>
  <p>
    At checkout you agree, by ticking the box and accepting the terms, that we may charge the card you save for
    <Brand name="care" /> at the monthly price above, every month after the free trial, until you cancel. We keep a record of
    that agreement. Your card details are held by our payment provider (Stripe), never by us. You can change the card or
    cancel anytime from your account ("Manage billing").
  </p>

  <h2>2. Reminder before you are charged</h2>
  <p>
    We will email you before the free period ends, telling you the date of the first payment and how to cancel.
  </p>

  <h2>3. What's included</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Voice conversations with the AI assistant, in all supported languages.</li>
    <li>Personas, the blue or white theme, and your conversation history in your account (export or delete anytime).</li>
    <li>Firmware updates over the air.</li>
    <li>{prices.interactionsPerMonth.toLocaleString("en-GB")} AI interactions per month (see section 3a).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3a. Monthly AI interactions</h2>
  <!-- LEGAL REVIEW: new wording (2026-10) describing the interaction allowance - to be reviewed by a professional. -->
  <ul>
    <li>
      <Brand name="care" /> includes {prices.interactionsPerMonth.toLocaleString("en-GB")} AI interactions in each monthly
      billing period, shared by all the watches on your account.
    </li>
    <li>
      One interaction is one request you make to the assistant — a question, a follow-up question, a note, a reminder or
      another voice command. A follow-up is a new request and counts separately. A web search, or any other tool the
      assistant uses to answer one request, does not use extra interactions.
    </li>
    <li>
      These do not use an interaction: silence or a recording in which nothing was understood; a request that fails
      because of a fault on our side or our AI partners' side; a request interrupted because the connection dropped;
      work the service does in the background (for example remembering what you asked it to). If you stop an answer
      yourself after your request was understood, that request counts.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your allowance renews every month: at the start of each monthly billing period and, during the free trial, every
      month from the day the trial starts. Unused interactions do not carry forward. Your account shows how many you have used, how many are
      left and when the allowance renews; we let you know when you reach 80% and 95%, and when it is used up.
    </li>
    <li>
      When the allowance is used up, the assistant does not answer new requests until it renews. Your saved notes and
      reminders (including their alarms), your account, watch settings and updates keep working; asking the assistant
      to change a note or reminder by voice is a request and needs an interaction. You can also buy {prices.topup.interactions} extra
      interactions for the rest of the current period ({formatPrice(prices.topup.GBP, "GBP")}, a one-off payment, never
      recurring); they end with that period.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you cancel, or your subscription ends, the assistant stops answering new requests at the end of the period you
      have paid for (or of the free trial), whatever interactions are left.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Cancelling</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel anytime from your account (Account, then "Manage billing"), which opens our payment provider's secure billing
    portal. The subscription then ends at the end of the current paid period (or of the free period) and you won't be
    charged again. You also have a 14-day right to cancel the subscription from the day the contract starts.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Price changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may change the price with at least 30 days' notice by email. If you don't agree, you can cancel before the new
    price applies.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Failed payments</h2>
  <p>
    If a payment fails we will email you and retry. If it still fails, the assistant stops answering until the payment
    is made.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Service availability</h2>
  <p>
    The assistant relies on our servers and our AI partners (OpenAI) and needs Wi-Fi. We work to keep the service
    available but can't guarantee it will be uninterrupted.
  </p>

  <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${config.supportEmail}`}>{config.supportEmail}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
